  "title": "Kourovka problem 6.10 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let p be a prime and n be an integer with p > 2n + 1. Let x, y be p-elements\nin GLn (C). If the subgroup ⟨x, y⟩ is finite, then it is an abelian p-group (W. Feit,\nJ. G. Thompson, Pacif. J. Math., 11, no. 4 (1961), 1257–1262). What can be said\nabout ⟨x, y⟩ in the case it is an infinite group?                         J. D. Dixon",
